  "description": "The 2026 general election for Arkansas's 1st Congressional District features four candidates: incumbent Republican Rep. Rick Crawford, Democrat Terri Yarbrough Green, Independent Jason Gaines, and Libertarian Steve Parsons. Crawford has held the seat since 2011 and became chair of the House Intelligence Committee in 2025. The district covers northeastern Arkansas and parts of the southeast, including Jonesboro, and has a strong Republican lean (+23R Cook PVI). All major nonpartisan forecasters rate the race as Safe or Solid Republican, though Democrats nationally are expected to be competitive for House control in 2026.",
